<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4542" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλῠδις</span></b> , Adv., (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλος</span>) 
			Ep.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλοσε,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>elsewhither,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλος, ἄ.
			ἄλλος</span> one <i>hither,</i> another <i>thither,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.486
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.71
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.980
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέπεται χρὼς ἄ.
			ἄλλῃ</span> his colour changes <i>now one way, now another,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.279
			</span></i>; imitated from <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> by <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				159.11
			</span></i>; later by itself, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				15.24.1
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Simm.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
